{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-203545-r4516597","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Hickory BBQ Pork Loin","sourcePageId":203545,"sourceRevision":"4516597","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T19:10:44Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Hickory%20BBQ%20Pork%20Loin&oldid=4516597","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:20.515Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for spice mixes","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chili powder","Category:Recipes using dark brown sugar","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using paprika","Category:Recipes using pepper","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using rosemary","Category:Recipes using thyme","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4870984e34b338d4b6f6ae2ad401c0f0fb3936746ddd2d630c7133abbab4d300","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pork recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n{{Warning|This recipe will generate sufficient carbon monoxide to poison you. Ensure the work space is safely ventilated.}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1 boneless [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] loin roast\n* Hickory chips\n\n=== '''Brine''' ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¾ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] cracked black [[Cookbook:Peppercorn|peppercorns]]\n* 2 cups very hot apple [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] ice\n\n=== '''Rub''' ===\n* 2 tbsp smoked [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n* 2 tbsp dark [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1 heaping tbsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* 1 tbsp cracked-black peppercorns\n* 1 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n* 2 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine all brine ingredients in a [[Cookbook:Gallon|gallon]]-size zip-top bag. Add pork roast and [[Cookbook:Brining|brine]] in the refrigerator for 3 hours.\n#Remove pork from brine. Pat dry with [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]] and set aside.\n#Combine rub ingredients. Massage into pork and refrigerate overnight.\n#The next day, place a roasting rack into a large roasting pan with a good amount of hickory chips in it. Insert a probe [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]] into the roast and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] at 200°F until internal temperature reaches 140°F.\n#Move to a plate and let rest uncovered 5 minutes. Serve thickly sliced.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for spice mixes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using paprika]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rosemary]]\n[[Category:Recipes using thyme]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Hickory BBQ Pork Loin","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 boneless pork loin roast","sourceText":"1 boneless pork loin roast","amountText":"1 boneless pork loin roast",